{%- comment -%}
  Dropmagic stylesheet carrier for the HEADER GROUP. Zero markup — its only job
  is to be `order[0]` of `header-group.json` so `dm-theme.css` is declared
  before any Dropmagic HTML on the page.

  WHY IT EXISTS. Section groups render from `layout/theme.liquid`, ahead of the
  body template that carries `dm-head`. Measured on a live product page
  (2026-09-10):

      82,956  </head>
      86,903  DM announcement bar   ┐ parsed and painted with
      90,800  DM header             ┘ no Dropmagic CSS at all
     109,551  <link dm-theme.css>   ← first declaration

  An in-body stylesheet blocks rendering of what FOLLOWS it, not what preceded
  it — so those 22.6 KB paint raw, then restyle. Visible signature: icon SVGs
  are emitted `width="100%" height="100%"` and carousel arrows are hidden by
  CSS alone (`data-arrows-show="false"`), so a missing stylesheet shows them
  full-bleed. Off the Dropmagic templates it is worse: `/collections/all` has
  no `dm-head` at all, so its only declaration was the one `dm-cart-drawer`
  emits from the FOOTER group, at byte 240,600 of 280,063.

  The fix is placement, not weight — dm-theme.css is 476 KB raw but 31 KB
  brotli behind a one-year `cache-control`.

  THE DUPLICATION IS THE RULE, NOT DEBT. `dm-head`, `dm-cart-drawer` and this
  file all declare the same two sheets, and all three keep them. Every root
  Dropmagic can render from — a page template, the header group, the footer
  group — is reached independently, so each one declares the CSS it needs
  rather than assuming a sibling got there first. `dm-cart-drawer.liquid` has
  carried that rule since it shipped; this file extends it to the header.

  It is also load-bearing, not just tidy. Engine `.liquid` files and
  `header-group.json` have INDEPENDENT writers: `sync-store-assets` pushes the
  whole engine set and stamps only `shopify_sync.engine`, while the group file
  is written by `publishPages` alone. Strip the declaration from `dm-head` and
  any store that gets the task without a publish has neither — an unstyled
  storefront with no way back until the merchant happens to publish. Some never
  will. So: never "consolidate" these into one declaration.

  Cost of holding the rule: two or three `<link>`s to one URL. That is one
  request, one shared parse, and one `RuleSet` in Blink — the thing to avoid is
  putting them on EVERY `dm-section` (a dozen-plus copies make style recalc walk
  a dozen copies of a 476 KB sheet), not the three roots.

  NOT the fonts. `dm-fonts` is a ~6 KB inline <style> (26 @font-face) already
  emitted twice per page; a third copy costs more than the swap it would save.
  The fix there is folding it into the per-store `dm-theme-vars.css`.

  NO markup, NO runtime JS. The dm-*.js set stays in `dm-head` — moving it here
  would ship 216 KB to every collection / cart / blog page. That the DM header's
  carousel and menu are currently inert on those pages is a real bug, and its
  own decision.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'dm-theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'dm-theme-vars.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- comment -%}
